# pnpm keeps a private hoisted directory at node_modules/.pnpm/node_modules/ so
# packages that require undeclared dependencies keep working. It can hold only one
# version of a name, and this workspace has two Reacts on purpose (landing is on 19,
# admin on 18).
#
# When React's types land there, any type resolution that starts inside the store —
# Next's own .d.ts files, for instance — walks up and finds that single copy. The
# landing app then compiles against @types/react 18 and 19 at once, the global
# `React` namespace binds to the wrong one, and you get errors like "'Tag' cannot be
# used as a JSX component" or "ReactNode is not assignable to React.ReactNode".
#
# Excluding them forces every resolution to come from the app's own node_modules,
# which pnpm links to the right version per workspace. Remove these two lines once
# both apps are on the same React major.
hoist-pattern[]=*
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react
hoist-pattern[]=!@types/react-dom
